Auto-context no longer puts files from a /cd-denied directory into the model's prompt. Before this, after /cd into a project whose .yoyo.toml denies a directory, read_file would refuse a file there, but auto-context (which runs on every REPL turn) could still attach it. It's committed as 9c44eba9, not pushed yet, and I commented the new register count on #869.

What changed
• The per-file decision moved out of auto_context_for_prompt into a new function, select_auto_context_paths, which takes the /cd deny list as a parameter. It calls path_guard_refusal_with, which checks the startup fence first (same results as before) and then the /cd list. The real function passes in the same list handle /rename uses.
• **The task assumed a shortcut that isn't there.** Step 1 expected an early return when there are no startup restrictions, like the one `/rename` had. This function has none: each check returns early on its own only when its list is empty, so a session with no startup fence still reaches the /cd check.
• **Test:** test_select_auto_context_paths_honours_cd_deny uses a local deny list and absolute temp paths, and compares the full returned list with assert_eq!:
  • with an empty `/cd` list, the result is unchanged from before;
  • denying secret with no startup restrictions excludes secret/f.rs, but secrets2/f.rs stays in, because matching is by path component, not by name prefix;
  • the same exclusion happens when unrelated startup restrictions are set.
• **Positive control:** I swapped the new call back to the old startup-only check and ran the test. It failed on the no-startup-restrictions case, then I restored the code.
• **Register: `src/commands_project.rs` came off `UNWIRED_CHECK_PATH_READERS`, which goes from 3 rows to 2**: src/context.rs and src/skill_fence.rs.
• **Size gate:** the file's entry in `tests/module_size.rs` is now 3709 (+56 from the 3653 starting count) with a dated Day 228 comment. That is inside the 100-line drift grace band.
• **Docs:** `permissions.md` now lists auto-context among the surfaces that honour the `/cd` list. I also changed its "other readers" sentence, which named "the project-description commands" as using the startup fence. That file had no other fence check, so the claim didn't match the code. I added a Day 228 note to ARCHITECTURE.md under commands_project.rs.

What's left on #869: besides those two register rows, /cd still doesn't reload [permissions] allow, [directories] allow, hooks, MCP servers or skills. My task file also listed permissions.deny reload as missing. According to permissions.md (I didn't open cd_deny to confirm), /cd already adds those patterns to bash's deny list, so I left it off the residue and said so in the commit and on #869.

Clippy (-D warnings), fmt and the full cargo test run passed before the last edits. Those edits only touched docs and ARCHITECTURE.md, and after them fmt, the module-size tests and the register guard passed again.
